--- parity notes (web/src/components/forms/PillFilterBar.tsx → native) ---
- Single-select WAI-ARIA tablist: container reports AutomationControlType.Tab carrying the caller-supplied ariaLabel
  (web role="tablist" aria-label); each pill reports AutomationControlType.TabItem + ISelectionItemProvider exposing
  aria-selected. Roving tabindex (web tabIndex={selected?0:-1}) → the active pill is the strip's single IsTabStop.
- Keyboard: Left/Right wrap around enabledKeys, Home/End jump to first/last enabled pill, disabled pills skipped
  (web handleKeyDown). Space/Enter and pointer tap pick (web onClick → onChange).
- Variants reproduced: pills (rounded-full chip + active fill + leading accent dot) and tabs (flat row + 2px accent
  underline + container bottom hairline). Six accents (cyan/green/amber/red/purple/blue) mapped to the brand chart
  palette brushes (TsChartRegen/Battery/Energy/Temperature/Power/Speed). Optional leading icon + optional muted
  "(count)" suffix (web `(${fmtInt(count)})` → locale-grouped N0). Disabled pill dimmed (opacity-40), non-interactive.
- States: the web source is a controlled presentational tablist (its only hook is useId, an id generator, not a data
  source), so it has no loading/error/stale/offline chrome — reproducing them would be drift. The honest branches are
  reproduced in full, plus a defensive empty branch (empty items → a locale-neutral em-dash marker, never a blank box).
- i18n: the web source declares no t() calls; its sole assistive string (ariaLabel) and every pill label are
  caller-composed/already-localized. No English literals are hardcoded in native code (the empty marker is a
  locale-neutral em dash). So the "every i18n key from source has a P1/S10 match" criterion is vacuously satisfied.
- Telemetry: emits view.opened slug=PillFilterBar on load (P1/S11), plus a PII-safe selection-changed signal (slug
  only, never a pill key/label/count).

